  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin obligated $10.8B in federal contract obligations during FY2026 to date, across 148 awards with an average award size of $73.2M. Lockheed Martin obligations are up 4.0% year over year. Lockheed Martin has grown obligations from $4.7B in FY21 to $10.8B in FY26, with FY22 at $7.1B, FY23 at $8.7B, FY24 at $7.3B, and FY25 at $10.4B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market for Lockheed Martin at $9.8B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M. Lockheed Martin also sells technical services and engineering work, including All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $42.8M. The top NAICS list shows concentrated manufacturing in missile and space systems alongside smaller streams in logistics, engineering, and specialized equipment manufacturing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Lockheed Martin obligations changed over time?",
        "body": "Lockheed Martin obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $10.8B in FY26. Lockheed Martin obligations increased to $7.1B in FY22 and $8.7B in FY23, then moved to $7.3B in FY24 and $10.4B in FY25. Lockheed Martin obligations are up 4.0% year over year in the current fiscal period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Lockheed Martin's top markets in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market for Lockheed Martin at $9.8B. Other notable markets for Lockheed Martin include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $42.8M."
      }
